  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICMPS 2025 Red TDT Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Strengthening advocacy voices: capacities, recognition and justice from the regional to the national level&quot; project in Mexico implemented by RED TDT,  aims to strenghten the organisational, communication and advocacy capacities of 500 human rights defenders in five regions of the country (north, west, centre, south and south-east). Priority will be given to indigenous defenders, community defenders, women defenders and organisations with less access to resources and visibility. Through training opportunities, collective analysis, and actions to raise awareness and public advocacy, social and political recognition of the work of defenders in contexts marked by violence, exclusion, and stigmatisation will be promoted</narrative>
  </description>
